    S04: { title: "RST for Supply Chain Resilience", subtitle: "Reverse Stress Testing for Supply Chain Resilience", authors: "Madison Smith, Michael Gaiewski, Sam Dulin, Laurel Williams, Jeffrey Keisler, Andrew Jin, Igor Linkov", date: "Related public preprint: Nov 2025; v2: 26 Nov 2025", kind: "Research preprint", level: "primary", doi: "https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.07289", readUrl: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.07289v2", access: "Open preprint; PDF linked from arXiv", evidence: "Preprint / version-specific model demonstration", verifiedOn: "2026-11-09", takeaway: "Start from a loss a decision maker cares about and infer upstream configurations, rather than only testing imagined hazards.", read: "Read the public abstract first, then the linked PDF's framework and discussion. The arXiv record pins v2 and gives both submission dates.", note: "The public record is a related preprint, not confirmation of journal publication or byte-identity with the supplied 22-page manuscript. Its abstract highlights Canada, Chile, and Mexico. Do not merge its findings with S05." },
